    deepLore: `Determined to reverse the catastrophic losses of the first day, Dhrishtadyumna arranged the Pandava army into the formidable Krauncha Vyuha (Heron formation), while Bhishma countered with the vast Maha Vyuha. \n\nThe second day saw the emergence of the youngest heroes. Abhimanyu, the 16-year-old son of Arjuna, rode furiously into the heart of the Kaurava army. Demonstrating martial mastery inherited from his father, he fearlessly engaged Grandfather Bhishma directly. The duel between the aged patriarch and the teenage prodigy stunned both armies. Abhimanyu actually managed to shatter Bhishma's bow, earning roaring applause from the Pandava camp.\n\nMeanwhile, Bhima bypassed the central commanders and targeted the fiercely loyal Kalinga army stationed on the Kaurava flanks. Armed with his colossal mace, Bhima waded into their infantry like a force of nature. King Srutayush of Kalinga charged Bhima with a massive elephant, but Bhima struck the beast so hard it collapsed, before executing the king and his son, Sakradeva. Bhima's rampage was so apocalyptic that the entire Kalinga battalion was annihilated, causing a massive rout in the Kaurava ranks.\n\nTo stall Bhima, Bhishma rushed to the flank, but he was intercepted by Satyaki and Dhrishtadyumna. Adding to the chaos, Ghatotkacha, Bhima's Rakshasa son, descended upon the battlefield. Using demonic illusions (Maya), Ghatotkacha created phantom beasts and terrifying apparitions that caused panic among Duryodhana's troops. By sunset on the second day, the Pandavas had successfully avenged their earlier losses, leaving Duryodhana deeply alarmed.`,
