    deepLore: `The fourth day witnessed brutal, close-quarters combat as the great military formations collapsed into a chaotic melee. The focus of the battle shifted intensely toward Bhima. Emboldened by his success on the second day, Bhima actively sought out Duryodhana's brothers, intent on fulfilling his terrible vow made in the dice hall to slaughter all 100 Kauravas.\n\nSpotting a group of Duryodhana's brothers, Bhima charged with reckless abandon. In a flurry of devastating mace strikes and bare-handed grappling, Bhima crushed eight of Dhritarashtra's sons to death in a matter of minutes. The sight of his brothers being slaughtered sent Duryodhana into a state of panic and fury. He immediately ordered a massive division of Magadha war elephants to stampede Bhima.\n\nUnfazed, Bhima leaped into the advancing herd, swinging his mace with such catastrophic force that skulls shattered and massive beasts were hurled into the air. When the elephant division was routed, King Bhagadatta—an ancient, formidable warrior and ally of the Kauravas—charged on his colossal, genetically superior elephant, Supratika. \n\nBhagadatta nearly trampled Bhima, but the fierce Rakshasa Ghatotkacha arrived in the nick of time, intercepting Supratika with his own dark magic. Ghatotkacha rode a phantom beast and unleashed terrifying illusions of fire and blood upon the Kaurava army, forcing Bhishma to call a general retreat as the sun set, realizing the demonic powers of Ghatotkacha were insurmountable in the fading light.`,
