    deepLore: `On the seventh day, the Kauravas deployed the Mandala Vyuha (Circular Formation), a highly defensive array. The Pandavas countered with the Vajra Vyuha (Thunderbolt Formation), designed to crack the circle open. \n\nThe day was marked by the terrifying martial dominance of Dronacharya and Grandfather Bhishma. Frustrated by the stalemate, Drona swept across the Pandava lines like a wildfire, invoking celestial astras that incinerated thousands of foot soldiers and chariot fighters with effortless mastery. Seeing the catastrophic loss of life, Dhrishtadyumna rushed forth to engage his former teacher. The clash was intensely personal; Dhrishtadyumna was born from a sacrificial fire with the sole cosmic destiny of severing Drona's head.\n\nDrona fought with unmatched fury, unleashing arrows that blotted out the sun, but Dhrishtadyumna bravely held his ground, deflecting the deadly strikes. Although Drona easily repelled Dhrishtadyumna's onslaught due to superior experience and divine weaponry, the fierce personal duel diverted Drona's attention long enough to save the wider Pandava army from total collapse.\n\nElsewhere on the field, the transgender warrior Shikhandi (the reincarnation of Princess Amba) repeatedly charged at Grandfather Bhishma. True to his vow, Bhishma completely ignored Shikhandi, refusing to even look at someone born as a woman. King Bhagadatta, riding his colossal elephant Supratika, engaged Ghatotkacha in a spectacular battle of brute force versus demonic illusion. The sun set with the Kauravas having gained a distinct tactical edge, leaving the Pandava camp gripped by anxiety.`,
