    deepLore: `Following the tragic fall of Grandfather Bhishma, the Kaurava camp was plunged into mourning. However, this also marked the return of Karna, who, freed from Bhishma's restriction, finally entered the battlefield, bringing renewed hope to Duryodhana. Duryodhana immediately appointed Dronacharya as the Supreme Commander.\n\nEager to prove his loyalty, Drona asked Duryodhana what boon he desired. Duryodhana cunningly replied, "Do not kill Yudhisthira. Capture him alive and bring him to me." Duryodhana's sinister logic was that if Yudhisthira were killed, Arjuna and Bhima would mercilessly slaughter everyone in revenge. But if Yudhisthira were captured alive, Duryodhana could simply force him into another rigged game of dice and send the Pandavas back into exile for another 13 years.\n\nDrona agreed, but he firmly stated, "I can only capture Yudhisthira if Arjuna is removed from the battlefield. As long as Arjuna is near, even the Gods cannot touch Yudhisthira." Hearing this, King Susharma and his brothers of the Trigarta kingdom—harboring a bitter grudge against Arjuna—took a terrifying oath. They formed a suicide squad known as the 'Samshaptakas', swearing to either kill Arjuna or die trying, deliberately challenging him at the farthest edges of the battlefield to draw him away from his eldest brother.\n\nWith Arjuna isolated miles away fighting the Samshaptakas, Drona unleashed his terrifying might on the Pandava center, attempting to capture Yudhisthira. The Pandava army panicked, but King Virat, Drupada, and Bhima formed a desperate physical wall around their king, barely managing to keep Drona at bay as the sun set on the eleventh day.`,
