    deepLore: `On the 12th day, the strategy remained the same: the Samshaptakas drew Arjuna away, while Drona launched a ferocious, highly calculated assault to capture Yudhisthira. Drona arranged his forces in the Garuda Vyuha and cut through the Pandava defenses with alarming speed. Yudhisthira found himself directly in Drona's crosshairs, and panic swept through the Pandava ranks.\n\nHowever, the day was defined by the intervention of King Bhagadatta, the ancient and formidable ruler of Pragjyotisha. Riding his colossal, genetically superior war-elephant Supratika, Bhagadatta wreaked absolute havoc, crushing Pandava battalions beneath the beast's feet. Hearing the destruction, Arjuna temporarily broke away from the Samshaptakas and rushed back to intercept Bhagadatta.\n\nA spectacular battle ensued. Realizing Arjuna's unmatched skill, Bhagadatta invoked the Vaishnavastra—an infallible celestial weapon of Lord Vishnu that guarantees the death of its target. He hurled it directly at Arjuna's chest. Knowing Arjuna could not survive it, Lord Krishna stood up in the chariot, offering His own chest to the weapon. Upon touching Krishna (who is an avatar of Vishnu), the deadly weapon peacefully transformed into a beautiful garland of flowers around Krishna's neck. With the threat neutralized, Arjuna shot an arrow that pierced the elephant's brain, and then severed Bhagadatta's bow, ultimately killing the ancient king and forcing Drona to retreat for the day.`,
